--- a/pupil/model/README.md
+++ b/pupil/model/README.md
@@ -10,3 +10,27 @@
   python -X utf8 make_training_list.py
   ```
   then, in MATLAB, `pupil_train_general('<work>\train_pairs.csv', 'model\general_pupil_unet.mat', 'Epochs', 12, 'TestCsv', '<work>\test_pairs.csv')` (about 40 min on a GPU).
+
+## current_rig_pupil_unet.mat (added 2026-11-15, current cohort 9669m / 9670f)
+
+`general_pupil_unet.mat` fine-tuned on frames of the current rig (1920x1080 side view, IC Capture). Use it with
+`"pupil_detector": "maxp"` and `"pupil_model": "pupil/model/current_rig_pupil_unet.mat"` in `run_all_config.json`.
+`general_pupil_unet.mat` is unchanged and is still the default.
+
+- **Training data.**
+  - 384 frames: 24 frames spread over each of the 16 day-1/day-2 sessions, all 8 mice, with the eye ROIs checked on 2026-11-15.
+  - Each frame was labelled by two independent visual labellers, who picked which candidate contour outlines the pupil, or said "pupil not visible". A third labeller decided the 93 frames where they disagreed.
+  - When both labellers chose a contour, they chose the same pupil in 97 % of the frames. They disagreed mostly on whether the pupil is visible at all: they agreed on that in 86 % of frames, and in only 0 % for day-2 9669m green1, a dark eye.
+  - Used for training: 196 frames with a well-fitting pupil contour, and 50 frames where the pupil is not visible (empty target).
+- **Training.**
+  - Same input as the general model: ROI crop, glint suppression, CLAHE, 128x128.
+  - Same generalized Dice loss and the same augmentation as `pupil_train_general.m`.
+  - Adam, learning rate 1e-4, 30 epochs, mini-batch 16, on the CPU (about 10 min).
+- **Checked on held-out data.** Folds held out 2 mice each, or one day. Results are on frames where both labellers agree (311 frames).
+  - Fine-tuned model with the `maxp` blob choice (the most probable blob, kept only if its probability is >= 0.9): finds the pupil in 82-83 % of the frames where it is visible. 22-24 % of its picks are wrong (another dark spot, or a pupil that is not visible).
+  - General model on the same frames: 44 % and 45 %.
+  - Errors cluster in the hard sessions: the inflamed or narrowed eyes of 9669m black and 9670f black, the dark day-2 eye of 9669m green1, and the dark spot under the upper lid of 9670f white.
+- **Limits.**
+  - Trained on days 1-2 of these 8 mice only.
+  - For a new cohort, or if the camera or IR light changes, label new frames and fine-tune again (scripts in `current_cohort_workflow/pupil_finetune/` of the analysis repo).
+  - The eye images of this rig are very dark: the eye ROI uses about 10-45 of 255 grey levels. More IR light or a higher camera exposure / gain would help any detector.
